<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Terminal / SCP Historical</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Discovery (audio recordings; scanned original documents; terminal)</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Perhaps there was a reason why the O5-Council decided to bury this information&#8230;</p>
<strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A Junior Researcher logs onto an older terminal and uncovers a forgotten SCP with deep roots in the SCP foundations history.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<strong>Central Narrative:</strong>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The SCP foundation has a questionable history, but this Junior Researcher attempts to solidify one of the oldest SCPs discovered by the Foundation. Compiling information from older terminals and transcribing paper archives, the SCP “Darkhouse” is reclassified as one of the earliest discovered SCPs. The SCP was “lost” when the Foundation transferred their data from paper to computers.</p>
<p>Dating back to 1792, the original Cape Henry Lighthouse was the first federally funded public works project of the newly formed United States government. In 1881, a new lighthouse was constructed to replace the original. With rising threats from around the world, both human and anomalous, the United States government attempted to utilize unexplainable properties the original lighthouse possessed.</p>
<p>The SCP “Darkhouse” ‘s anomalous properties are charged by UVA (315-400 nm) and UVB (280-315 nm) Ultraviolet radiation. The radiation appears to activate the anomalous properties, causing the SCP “Darkhouse” to enter an “active” state. During this state, the SCP “Darkhouse” will project a photon-absorbing substance, blocking all light it encompasses. Effects of the substance on living organisms have been redacted due to its tendencies to <em>dissolve and dissipate matter.</em> Containment procedures have been automated and the SCP “Darkhouse” has not been attended to by Foundation personnel since its original containment.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<strong>Additional Notes:</strong> “It doesn’t shine, it shadows…”
