<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Psychological&#8230; something</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> A normal SCP article, but it's split into two distinct sections</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The SCP itself is more or less the designation for two separate scenarios. In scenario A, the SCP is a Euclid SCP, who's a young human girl, a bit distorted from reality, and makes half of the people who know of her think she doesn't actually exist.<br />
In scenario B, the SCP is an infohazardous memetic effect, which makes half of the people who know of it think that there's a person there, who really isn't.<br />
The memetic effect of either scenario is so powerful, and so overwhelming, that despite their best efforts, the foundation can't tell which one is true, so they've documented it as if it's neither and both at the same time.<br />
After all, it's impossible to prove either way</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The main narrative is gonna come from how the scenario A SCP is mentally affected by her affliction, and how she may have gotten like this based on interviews with her and the like<br />
Also, it's going to focus on how this uncertainty is affecting the foundation personnel who know of the SCP, including conflicts starting due to people in scenario A starting fights with people in scenario B<br />
People are getting angry about a whole humanoid containment chamber which is going completely unused</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> the main hook is obviously the esoterics of something that can't be proven to exist or not exist, and possibly how the foundation reacts to encountering something that they can't truly understand despite their best efforts. I'd imagine people would already be interested as soon as they see &quot;<strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid / Keter (?)&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I guess above all else I want to know if this concept has been done before and if so I would like to know how to make it more unique.<br />
Also, I just wanna know if it's good or not alltogether</p>

